Alembic/Flask-Migrate schema migrations for Salfanet NMS.

## Status

`2169e93c7970_baseline_...py` is a baseline migration autogenerated from the
models as of 2026-09-01 — it was NOT here before. `app.py` still runs its own
`migrate_schema()` (raw `ALTER TABLE ADD COLUMN`, best-effort) on every server
start; that has NOT been removed or disabled by adding this. The two systems
are independent for now — this baseline exists so future schema changes can
be made as proper, reviewable, versioned migrations instead of by hand-editing
`migrate_schema()`.

## One-time setup per existing deployment

An existing database already has all current tables (created via
`db.create_all()` + `migrate_schema()`), so running `flask db upgrade` against
it would try to `CREATE TABLE` on tables that already exist and fail. Instead,
mark it as already being at the baseline, without executing anything:

```
FLASK_APP=app.py flask db stamp head
```

A **new** deployment can do this instead of relying on `db.create_all()`:

```
FLASK_APP=app.py flask db upgrade
```

## Going forward

For a genuinely new schema change, prefer:

```
FLASK_APP=app.py flask db migrate -m "add x column to y"
# review the generated file in versions/ before committing
FLASK_APP=app.py flask db upgrade
```

over adding another `ALTER TABLE` to `migrate_schema()` in app.py.
